    "notes": "The exact Gejekapublic-domain exterior confirms the pale church, broad ribbed bell dome, tiered south portal, separate west entrance, adjacent arcaded/windowed long facade and paired tall end turrets. The exact Szilas2007CC0 courtyard view confirms the two-storey chamfered cloister, broad open bays with three lower shafts and paired upper lights, open gallery depth, medallion parapets and conical pinnacles. Current whole, full-front, church/dome, cloister and paired-turret renders retain those identifying forms. The distant western facade, hidden north rooms/rear roofs, bay counts and intermediate dimensions remain mapped/architectural estimates; fine figural/foliate carving, inscriptions and interior vaulting are outside scope. No reference pixels are embedded."
